 "notes": "Pass A, blind. Lines: left page 21 text lines (L1..L21, incl. small interlinear cipher line L9 squeezed under L8) + a marginal cipher insertion in the gutter area to the right of L16 ('+ 85.π.38.68.33.32 / 95'), placed in reading order right after L16's last token '2' (the '+' at the end of L16 and at the start of the insertion is an insertion/reference mark; kept once as SYM:autre-plus? — probably NOT a cipher sign, drop it if so). Right page 22 lines (R1..R22).\nSymbol conventions: SYM:psi = the very frequent sign written as an open cup with a vertical stem through it (ψ/φ-like; I first read it as φ; all instances treated as one sign). SYM:q-barré = 9/q with crossbar on the descender. SYM:K = cursive k. SYM:w = w/ɯ-like sign (some instances look like 'm' with a tail, 'ɯ'; all lumped as w). SYM:pi = π (sometimes looks like τ). SYM:x = x. SYM:u = u (L19). SYM:mars = σ/o with a small arrow to upper right (L20 clear; R7 instance only a tick, hence mars?). SYM:8-barré = 8 with a slash (R19). SYM:livre? = first sign of R1, a t/l-like stroke with a double crossbar (£/ŧ-like). SYM:l-cursif = looped l (R1). SYM:autre-a-psi-ligature? (L11) = an 'a'/'u'-like loop joined to a psi with doubled stem; could be two signs (e.g. u + psi) or one special sign.\nMarks: tilde = wavy stroke above; macron = flat bar or flat arc above (often with a small hook at one end) — the writer's over-strokes vary between a clear wave and a flat arc, so tilde vs macron is the main uncertainty (flagged '?'); acute = short slanted stroke above; caron = small u/v-shaped hook above (breve-like); diaeresis = two dots; dot = single dot.\nDOTTED 1: the digit 1 is often written like an 'i' with a dot. Where a dot sits over a 1 I recorded '|dot?' (or 'diaeresis?' when two dots); this may be just the letterform rather than a cipher mark — treat these with caution.\nDigit 0 is written as a small 'o'/'ʋ' with a tick (e.g. 30, 40, 80); 5 is written like a long s 'ʃ'.\nSpecific doubts: L1 '80' (could be 86); L6 '54' (first digit ʃ = 5); L16 final '2' is written low/small (2|none?); L20 '32|other' = a small 3-like curl written above 32 (unclear mark type); R18 '73' has an ink blot over it with a stroke (acute?); R18 '51' (could be 55); R3 first sign '6' alone (single digit, 6 with hook); L8 '1' and '2' single-digit signs with two dots each. L5 '29' partly covered by a stain but legible.\nLine-end dashes/flourishes and the right-margin archival/blue pencil foliation are not transcribed. A '+' written between R14/R15 ('escrit + le plus') is an insertion mark in the clear text, not transcribed as a sign.\nClear text is a rough diplomatic reading for anchoring only.",
